{"name":"Mesopotamian Dagger","hex":"#804040","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dagger","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stabbing weapon, similar to a sword but with a short, double-edged blade.","The typographical mark †."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pierce with a dagger; to stab.","To perform the daggering dance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dagger"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mesopotamia","blocks":[{"text":"Mesopotamia is a historical region of West Asia situated within the Tigris–Euphrates river system, in the northern part of the Fertile Crescent. It corresponds roughly to the territory of modern Iraq. Just beyond it lies southwestern Iran, where the region transitions into the Iranian plateau, marking the shift from the Arab world to Iran."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/N-Mesopotamia_and_Syria_english.svg/330px-N-Mesopotamia_and_Syria_english.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamia","wikidata":"Q11767"},{"title":"Dagger","blocks":[{"text":"A dagger is a fighting knife typically with a very sharp point and usually one or two sharp edges, typically designed or capable of being used as a cutting or thrusting weapon. Daggers have been used throughout human history for close combat confrontations, and many cultures have used adorned daggers in ritual and ceremonial contexts. The dagger's distinctive shape and historic usage have made it iconic and symbolic. In the modern sense, a dagger is designed for close-proximity combat or self-defense; due to its use in historic weapon assemblages, it has associations with assassination and murder. However, double-edged knives play different roles in different social contexts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Fs-dagger.jpg/330px-Fs-dagger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagger","wikidata":"Q182780"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Mesopotamia_9_October_2020.jpg/500px-Mesopotamia_9_October_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Mesopotamia_9_October_2020.jpg/1280px-Mesopotamia_9_October_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Mesopotamia_9_October_2020.jpg/500px-Mesopotamia_9_October_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMesopotamia_9_October_2020.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Berl%C3%ADn_Ishtar_05.JPG/500px-Berl%C3%ADn_Ishtar_05.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Berl%C3%ADn_Ishtar_05.JPG/1280px-Berl%C3%ADn_Ishtar_05.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Berl%C3%ADn_Ishtar_05.JPG/500px-Berl%C3%ADn_Ishtar_05.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABerl%C3%ADn_Ishtar_05.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Mosul_river.jpg/500px-Mosul_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Mosul_river.jpg/1280px-Mosul_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Mosul_river.jpg/500px-Mosul_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Tigris river flowin